# stage0 never treats a loop as a terminator: `while true:` with no break still gets
# "may fall through without returning a value". stage1 special-cased it as a terminator
# (claiming parity it did not have), so semantic analysis passed the function and the
# BACKEND declined it instead — rc=2 "backend emitted no functions for this unit",
# a compiler limitation reported in place of the user's actual defect.
def f() -> i64:
    while true:
        pass
